  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">BIRN St&#xf6;d till unders&#xf6;kande journalistik 2022- 2026</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">BIRN, Support to investigative journalism 2022-2026 - BIRN, Media freedom</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Programmet, Balkan Investigative Reporting Network Macedonia 2022&#x2013;2025, syftar till att &#xe5;terst&#xe4;lla allm&#xe4;nhetens f&#xf6;rtroende f&#xf6;r medier i Nordmakedonien, bidra till &#xf6;kad transparens och h&#xe5;lla myndigheter ansvariga genom h&#xf6;gkvalitativ journalistik samt till att utbilda nya journalister till att fungera som vakthundar &#xf6;ver den unga demokratin. De tv&#xe5; m&#xe5;len i programmet &#xe4;r att 1) ge allm&#xe4;nheten tillg&#xe5;ng till trov&#xe4;rdig information som g&#xf6;r det m&#xf6;jligt f&#xf6;r dem att fatta v&#xe4;lgrundade beslut, delta i demokratiska processer och st&#xe4;lla myndigheter till svars samt 2) bidra till att st&#xe4;rka h&#xf6;gkvalitativ, faktabaserad rapportering samt n&#xe4;tverkande mellan medier och bygga upp kapacitet bland unga journalister.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program aims to restore the public trust in media, boost transparency and hold authorities accountable by producing high quality journalism and to train new journalists to serve as watchdogs over the young democracy.

Balkan Investigative Reporting Network (BIRN) Macedonia is an independent NGO, founded in 2004. The two objectives are 1) provide the public with access to credible information that enables them to make informed decisions and participate in democratic processes and hold authorities accountable, 2) contribute to strengthening high quality, fact-based reporting, as well as networking of media, and building capacity among young journalists.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program has two objectives: i) Provide the public with access to credible information that enables them to make informed decisions and participate in democratic processes and hold authorities accountable and ii) contribute to strengthening capacities of media, strengthen professional reporting standards and ethics among journalists that leads to higher quality reporting and restore interest in the profession.</narrative>
  </description>
